  "id": "DrugBank_DB12141 - MONDO_18437",
  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a shared pathway involving Idarubicin, which is indicated for both AML with maturation and AML with Npm1 somatic mutations. The evidence suggests that Gilteritinib may be a potential therapeutic agent for AML with Npm1 mutations, as it shares a common indication with Idarubicin in these cases. The presence of a direct indication from Gilteritinib to AML with Npm1 mutations is supported by the indirect pathway through Idarubicin, which is indicated for both AML with maturation and AML with Npm1 mutations. This indicates that Gilteritinib may have a role in treating AML with Npm1 mutations, possibly through a mechanism that involves the same therapeutic targets as Idarubicin. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Gilteritinib to be repurposed for AML with Npm1 mutations, based on its shared indication with Idarubicin in these conditions.",
